# Illustration

Use an illustration to explain a task or a relationship. An illustration is not a device state, a photograph, a chart or a replacement for Home Assistant’s familiar icons. civica draws its own artwork and does not reuse government identity assets.

## Section headers and homepage cards

Use the original header family on the seven section landing pages and on the Colour, Data and Illustration guides. Detailed component pages keep their space for rendered examples. Each scene explains its section: typography and swatches for Styles, reusable controls for Components, a connected task sequence for Patterns.

The Styles, Components and Patterns homepage cards reuse the geometry of their section header. Keep that link when either asset changes. A header is 640 by 480 and a homepage card is 320 by 140. Show the whole header illustration without cropping or distortion, beside the heading and introduction on wide screens (minimum height 450 pixels) and below them on narrow screens. Do not put headings in the image.

These illustrations repeat the introduction beside them, so the page images have empty alternatives. The [artwork register](../reference/documentation-artwork.json) records a description for informative reuse, the editable sources, the five-colour palette and the review evidence. An illustration is never the only explanation or navigation label. Its pale background sits beside the dark blue text panel and does not change with a household palette.

